] [17592186291991 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186291399 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186291991 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "54c026e3-b2cd-5614-8267-7aebb7db7238" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186291996 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186291072 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186291996 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045492 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186291996 #edb/ref 1077 "field-1" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186291996 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186291072 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186291996 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "55e50f30-5144-5fc9-bbe4-2c993c917c8d" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186292311 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186291350 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186292311 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045492 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186292311 #edb/ref 1077 "field-1" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186292311 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186291350 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186292311 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "bbe60cfe-5f51-58fc-bd9d-0958798e7eaa" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186292370 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186291644 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186292370 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045492 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186292370 #edb/ref 1077 "field-1" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186292370 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186291644 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186292370 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "d2211671-c87b-5af3-925c-c70df0bb7ccf" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186292402 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186290968 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186292402 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045492 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186292402 #edb/ref 1077 "field-1" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186292402 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186290968 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186292402 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "d970493d-b5a8-5591-ae32-1929a0baff29" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186292467 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186291417 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186292467 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045492 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186292467 #edb/ref 1077 "field-2" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186292467 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186291417 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186292467 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "e9197374-8ffc-5179-b8a7-723e02b609fd" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186292511 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186291718 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186292511 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045492 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186292511 #edb/ref 1077 "field-1" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186292511 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186291718 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186292511 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "f8196514-e01e-53a8-87c9-b13f0f9aa45e" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186292565 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186292311 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186292565 #edb/ref 1069 "q-256466" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186292565 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186292565 #edb/ref 1071 "Suppose we wish to find a root of the function $f(x)={x}^{3}+3{x}^{2}-2$ in the interval $[-2,0].$ Calculate one iteration of the Newton-Raphson process starting from the point ${x}_{0}=-1.2.$ Round your answer to three decimal places.\n\n${x}_{1}≈$\n{{field-1}}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186292565 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "4b69ecb8-18be-5795-8ca2-bd6abf263b3a" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186292565 #edb/ref 1074 "The formula for the Newton-Raphson method is\n\n$$\n{x}_{n+1}={x}_{n}-\\frac{f({x}_{n})}{{f}^{′}({x}_{n})}\n$$\n\nwhere ${f}^{′}({x}_{n})$ is the derivative of $f(x)$ evaluated at ${x}_{n}.$\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\n{f}^{′}(x)=({x}^{3}+3{x}^{2}-2)^{′}=3{x}^{2}+6x.\n$$\n\nTherefore, our Newton-Raphson formula is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{n+1} & ={x}_{n}-\\frac{{x}_{n}^{3}+3{x}_{n}^{2}-2}{3{x}_{n}^{2}+6{x}_{n}} \\\\  & =\\frac{{x}_{n}(3{x}_{n}^{2}+6{x}_{n})-({x}_{n}^{3}+3{x}_{n}^{2}-2)}{3{x}_{n}^{2}+6{x}_{n}} \\\\  & =\\frac{2{x}_{n}^{3}+3{x}_{n}^{2}+2}{3{x}_{n}^{2}+6{x}_{n}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nStarting with ${x}_{0}=-1.2,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} & =\\frac{2{x}_{0}^{3}+3{x}_{0}^{2}+2}{3{x}_{0}^{2}+6{x}_{0}} \\\\  & =\\frac{2(-1.2)^{3}+3(-1.2)^{2}+2}{3(-1.2)^{2}+6(-1.2)} \\\\  & =\\frac{2.864}{(-2.88)} \\\\  & ≈-0.994,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nrounded to three decimal places." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186292568 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186291988 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186292568 #edb/ref 1069 "q-256499" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186292568 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186292568 #edb/ref 1071 "Suppose we wish to find a root of the function $f(x)={x}^{4}-10{x}^{2}+8$ in the interval $[0,1].$ Calculate the second iteration of the Newton-Raphson process starting from the point ${x}_{0}=0.5.$ Round your answer to three decimal places.\n\n${x}_{2}≈$\n{{field-1}}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186292568 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "0e48e9bd-4f64-588a-8bbc-610b3e1586aa" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186292568 #edb/ref 1074 "The formula for the Newton-Raphson method is\n\n$$\n{x}_{n+1}={x}_{n}-\\frac{f({x}_{n})}{{f}^{′}({x}_{n})}\n$$\n\nwhere ${f}^{′}({x}_{n})$ is the derivative of $f(x)$ evaluated at ${x}_{n}.$\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\n{f}^{′}(x)=({x}^{4}-10{x}^{2}+8)^{′}=4{x}^{3}-20x.\n$$\n\nTherefore, our Newton-Raphson formula is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{n+1} & ={x}_{n}-\\frac{{x}_{n}^{4}-10{x}_{n}^{2}+8}{4{x}_{n}^{3}-20{x}_{n}} \\\\  & =\\frac{{x}_{n}(4{x}_{n}^{3}-20{x}_{n})-({x}_{n}^{4}-10{x}_{n}^{2}+8)}{4{x}_{n}^{3}-20{x}_{n}} \\\\  & =\\frac{3{x}_{n}^{4}-10{x}_{n}^{2}-8}{4{x}_{n}^{3}-20{x}_{n}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nStarting with ${x}_{0}=0.5,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} & =\\frac{3{x}_{0}^{4}-10{x}_{0}^{2}-8}{4{x}_{0}^{3}-20{x}_{0}} \\\\  & =\\frac{3(0.5)^{4}-10(0.5)^{2}-8}{4(0.5)^{3}-20(0.5)} \\\\  & =1.085\\,526…\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFor the second iteration, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{2} & =\\frac{3{x}_{n}^{4}-10{x}_{n}^{2}-8}{4{x}_{n}^{3}-20{x}_{n}} \\\\  & =\\frac{3(1.085\\,526…)^{4}-10(1.085\\,526…)^{2}-8}{4(1.085\\,526…)^{3}-20(1.085\\,526…)} \\\\  & ≈0.941,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nrounded to three decimal places." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186292570 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186291832 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186292570 #edb/ref 1069 "q-256510" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186292570 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186292570 #edb/ref 1071 "Suppose we wish to find a root of the function $f(x)={x}^{4}-2x-1$ in the interval $[1,2].$ Calculate the second iteration of the Newton-Raphson process starting from the point ${x}_{0}=1.5.$ Round your answer to three decimal places.\n\n${x}_{2}≈$\n{{field-1}}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186292570 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "8c4fa760-3256-5c22-b663-79a18f288418" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186292570 #edb/ref 1074 "The formula for the Newton-Raphson method is\n\n$$\n{x}_{n+1}={x}_{n}-\\frac{f({x}_{n})}{{f}^{′}({x}_{n})}\n$$\n\nwhere ${f}^{′}({x}_{n})$ is the derivative of $f(x)$ evaluated at ${x}_{n}.$\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\n{f}^{′}(x)=({x}^{4}-2x-1)^{′}=4{x}^{3}-2.\n$$\n\nTherefore, our Newton-Raphson formula is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{n+1} & ={x}_{n}-\\frac{{x}^{4}-2x-1}{4{x}_{n}^{3}-2} \\\\  & =\\frac{{x}_{n}(4{x}_{n}^{3}-2)-({x}_{n}^{4}-2{x}_{n}-1)}{4{x}_{n}^{3}-2} \\\\  & =\\frac{3{x}_{n}^{4}+1}{4{x}_{n}^{3}-2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nStarting with ${x}_{0}=1.5,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} & =\\frac{3{x}_{0}^{4}+1}{4{x}_{0}^{3}-2} \\\\  & =\\frac{3(1.5)^{4}+1}{4(1.5)^{3}-2} \\\\  & =1.407\\,608…\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFor the second iteration, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{2} & =\\frac{3{x}_{1}^{4}-1}{4{x}_{1}^{3}-2} \\\\  & =\\frac{3(1.407\\,608…)^{4}-1}{4(1.407\\,608…)^{3}-2} \\\\  & ≈1.396,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nrounded to three decimal places." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186292578 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186292370 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186292578 #edb/ref 1069 "q-256582" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186292578 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186292578 #edb/ref 1071 "Given that the function $f(x)={x}^{3}+4x-6$ has a root in the interval $[0,2],$ use the Newton-Raphson process starting from ${x}_{0}=1.3$ to estimate the root. Round your final answer to two decimal places.\n\n$x≈$\n{{field-1}}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186292578 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "013fb993-c34e-58d5-ab5a-96a9dfc2d8f4" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186292578 #edb/ref 1074 "The formula for the Newton-Raphson method is\n\n$$\n{x}_{n+1}={x}_{n}-\\frac{f({x}_{n})}{{f}^{′}({x}_{n})}\n$$\n\nwhere ${f}^{′}({x}_{n})$ is the derivative of $f(x)$ evaluated at ${x}_{n}.$\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\n{f}^{′}(x)=({x}^{3}+4x-6)^{′}=3{x}^{2}+4.\n$$\n\nTherefore, our Newton-Raphson formula is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{n+1} & ={x}_{n}-\\frac{{x}_{n}^{3}+4{x}_{n}-6}{3{x}_{n}^{2}+4} \\\\  & =\\frac{{x}_{n}(3{x}_{n}^{2}+4)-({x}_{n}^{3}+4{x}_{n}-6)}{3{x}_{n}^{2}+4} \\\\  & =\\frac{2{x}_{n}^{3}+6}{3{x}_{n}^{2}+4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nStarting with ${x}_{0}=1.3,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} & =\\frac{2{x}_{0}^{3}+6}{3{x}_{0}^{2}+4} \\\\  & =\\frac{2(1.3)^{3}+6}{3(1.3)^{2}+4} \\\\  & =1.145…\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSimilarly, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{2} & =\\frac{2{x}_{1}^{3}+6}{3{x}_{1}^{2}+4} \\\\  & =\\frac{2(1.145…)^{3}+6}{3(1.145…)^{2}+4} \\\\  & =1.134…, \\\\ {x}_{3} & =\\frac{2{x}_{2}^{3}+6}{3{x}_{2}^{2}+4} \\\\  & =\\frac{2(1.134…)^{3}+6}{3(1.134…)^{2}+4} \\\\  & =1.134….\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNotice that the last two approximations ${x}_{2}≈1.13$ and ${x}_{3}≈1.13$ are the same when rounded to two decimal places.\n\nTherefore, the root of the function is $x≈1.13,$ rounded to two decimal places." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186292580 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186292511 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186292580 #edb/ref 1069 "q-256588" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186292580 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186292580 #edb/ref 1071 "Given that the function $f(x)={x}^{3}-x-1$ has a root in the interval $[0,2],$ use the Newton-Raphson process starting from ${x}_{0}=1.5$ to estimate the root. Round your final answer to two decimal places.\n\n$x≈$\n{{field-1}}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186292580 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "09d5d54f-fddc-5f68-b1ba-4119ada7542d" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186292580 #edb/ref 1074 "The formula for the Newton-Raphson method is\n\n$$\n{x}_{n+1}={x}_{n}-\\frac{f({x}_{n})}{{f}^{′}({x}_{n})}\n$$\n\nwhere ${f}^{′}({x}_{n})$ is the derivative of $f(x)$ evaluated at ${x}_{n}.$\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\n{f}^{′}(x)=({x}^{3}-x-1)^{′}=3{x}^{2}-1.\n$$\n\nTherefore, our Newton-Raphson formula is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{n+1} & ={x}_{n}-\\frac{{x}_{n}^{3}-{x}_{n}-1}{3{x}_{n}^{2}-1} \\\\  & =\\frac{{x}_{n}(3{x}_{n}^{2}-1)-({x}_{n}^{3}-{x}_{n}-1)}{3{x}_{n}^{2}-1} \\\\  & =\\frac{2{x}_{n}^{3}+1}{3{x}_{n}^{2}-1}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nStarting with ${x}_{0}=1.5,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} & =\\frac{2{x}_{0}^{3}+1}{3{x}_{0}^{2}-1} \\\\  & =\\frac{2(1.5)^{3}+1}{3(1.5)^{2}-1} \\\\  & =1.347….\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSimilarly, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{2} & =\\frac{2{x}_{1}^{3}+1}{3{x}_{1}^{2}-1} \\\\  & =\\frac{2(1.347…)^{3}+1}{3(1.347…)^{2}-1} \\\\  & =1.325…, \\\\ {x}_{3} & =\\frac{2{x}_{2}^{3}+1}{3{x}_{2}^{2}-1} \\\\  & =\\frac{2(1.325…)^{3}+1}{3(1.325…)^{2}-1} \\\\  & =1.324…, \\\\ {x}_{4} & =\\frac{2{x}_{3}^{3}+1}{3{x}_{3}^{2}-1} \\\\  & =\\frac{2(1.324…)^{3}+1}{3(1.324…)^{2}-1} \\\\  & =1.324….\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNotice that the last two approximations ${x}_{3}≈1.32$ and ${x}_{4}≈1.32$ are the same when rounded to two decimal places.\n\nTherefore, the root of the function is $x≈1.32,$ rounded to two decimal places." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186292582 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186291991 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186292582 #edb/ref 1069 "q-256604" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186292582 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186292582 #edb/ref 1071 "Given that the function $f(x)={x}^{3}-x-4$ has a root in the interval $[1,2],$ use the Newton-Raphson process starting from ${x}_{0}=1.5$ to estimate the root. Round your final answer to one decimal place.\n\n$x≈$\n{{field-1}}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186292582 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "ce1e65e3-3237-5496-b03f-b34039bbc935" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186292582 #edb/ref 1074 "The formula for the Newton-Raphson method is\n\n$$\n{x}_{n+1}={x}_{n}-\\frac{f({x}_{n})}{{f}^{′}({x}_{n})}\n$$\n\nwhere ${f}^{′}({x}_{n})$ is the derivative of $f(x)$ evaluated at ${x}_{n}.$\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\n{f}^{′}(x)=({x}^{3}-x-4)^{′}=3{x}^{2}-1.\n$$\n\nTherefore, our Newton-Raphson formula is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{n+1} & ={x}_{n}-\\frac{{x}_{n}^{3}-x-4}{3{x}_{n}^{2}-1} \\\\  & =\\frac{{x}_{n}(3{x}_{n}^{2}-1)-({x}_{n}^{3}-{x}_{n}-4)}{3{x}_{n}^{2}-1} \\\\  & =\\frac{2{x}_{n}^{3}+4}{3{x}_{n}^{2}-1}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nStarting with ${x}_{0}=1.5,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} & =\\frac{2{x}_{0}^{3}+4}{3{x}_{0}^{2}-1} \\\\  & =\\frac{2(1.5)^{3}+4}{3(1.5)^{2}-1} \\\\  & =1.869…\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSimilarly, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{2} & =\\frac{2{x}_{1}^{3}+4}{3{x}_{1}^{2}-1} \\\\  & =\\frac{2(1.869…)^{3}+4}{3(1.869…)^{2}-1} \\\\  & =1.799…, \\\\ {x}_{3} & =\\frac{2{x}_{2}^{3}+4}{3{x}_{2}^{2}-1} \\\\  & =\\frac{2(1.799…)^{3}+4}{3(1.799…)^{2}-1} \\\\  & =1.796….\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNotice that the last two approximations ${x}_{2}≈1.8$ and ${x}_{3}≈1.8$ are the same when rounded to one decimal place.\n\nTherefore, the root of the function is $x≈1.8,$ rounded to one decimal place." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186292584 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186292402 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186292584 #edb/ref 1069 "q-256612" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186292584 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186292584 #edb/ref 1071 "Given that the function $f(x)={x}^{4}-8x-3$ has a root in the interval $[1,3],$ use the Newton-Raphson process starting from ${x}_{0}=2$ to estimate the root. Round your final answer to two decimal places.\n\n$x≈$\n{{field-1}}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186292584 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "79ea7f86-725b-5ac1-990c-02d59dacbbed" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186292584 #edb/ref 1074 "The formula for the Newton-Raphson method is\n\n$$\n{x}_{n+1}={x}_{n}-\\frac{f({x}_{n})}{{f}^{′}({x}_{n})}\n$$\n\nwhere ${f}^{′}({x}_{n})$ is the derivative of $f(x)$ evaluated at ${x}_{n}.$\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\n{f}^{′}(x)=({x}^{4}-8x-3)^{′}=4{x}^{3}-8.\n$$\n\nTherefore, our Newton-Raphson formula is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{n+1} & ={x}_{n}-\\frac{{x}_{n}^{4}-8{x}_{n}-3}{4{x}_{n}^{3}-8} \\\\  & =\\frac{{x}_{n}(4{x}_{n}^{3}-8)-({x}_{n}^{4}-8{x}_{n}-3)}{4{x}_{n}^{3}-8} \\\\  & =\\frac{3({x}_{n}^{4}+1)}{4({x}_{n}^{3}-2)}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nStarting with ${x}_{0}=2,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} & =\\frac{3({x}_{0}^{4}+1)}{4({x}_{0}^{3}-2)} \\\\  & =\\frac{3({2}^{4}+1)}{4({2}^{3}-2)} \\\\  & =\\frac{51}{24} \\\\  & =2.125.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSimilarly, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{2} & =\\frac{3({x}_{1}^{4}+1)}{4({x}_{1}^{3}-2)} \\\\  & =\\frac{3((2.125)^{4}+1)}{4((2.125)^{3}-2)} \\\\  & =2.112…, \\\\ {x}_{3} & =\\frac{3({x}_{2}^{4}+1)}{4({x}_{2}^{3}-2)} \\\\  & =\\frac{3((2.112…)^{4}+1)}{4((2.112…)^{3}-2)} \\\\  & =2.111….\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNotice that the last two approximations ${x}_{2}≈2.11$ and ${x}_{3}≈2.11$ are the same when rounded to two decimal places.\n\nTherefore, the root of the function is $x≈2.11,$ rounded to two decimal places." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186292587 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186291996 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186292587 #edb/ref 1069 "q-256623" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186292587 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186292587 #edb/ref 1071 "Suppose we wish to find a root of the function $f(x)={e}^{-x}+{x}^{3}-2x$ in the interval $[0,1].$ Calculate one iteration of the Newton-Raphson process starting from the point ${x}_{0}=0.5.$ Round your answer to three decimal places.\n\n${x}_{1}≈$\n{{field-1}}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186292587 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "31695794-a02a-5139-9ef2-dcc26171634b" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186292587 #edb/ref 1074 "The formula for the Newton-Raphson method is\n\n$$\n{x}_{n+1}={x}_{n}-\\frac{f({x}_{n})}{{f}^{′}({x}_{n})}\n$$\n\nwhere ${f}^{′}({x}_{n})$ is the derivative of $f(x)$ evaluated at ${x}_{n}.$\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\n{f}^{′}(x)=({e}^{-x}+{x}^{3}-2x)^{′}=-{e}^{-x}+3{x}^{2}-2.\n$$\n\nTherefore, our Newton-Raphson formula is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{n+1} & ={x}_{n}-\\frac{{e}^{-{x}_{n}}+{x}_{n}^{3}-2{x}_{n}}{-{e}^{-{x}_{n}}+3{x}_{n}^{2}-2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nStarting with ${x}_{0}=0.5,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} & ={x}_{0}-\\frac{{e}^{-{x}_{0}}+{x}_{0}^{3}-2{x}_{0}}{-{e}^{-{x}_{0}}+3{x}_{0}^{2}-2} \\\\  & =0.5-\\frac{{e}^{-0.5}+{0.5}^{3}-2\\cdot 0.5}{-{e}^{-0.5}+3\\cdot {0.5}^{2}-2} \\\\  & ≈0.355,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nrounded to three decimal places." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186552887 #edb/ref 1080 "5.943" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186552887 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186552887 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "0eff231e-6f95-5871-b9f1-0a3ff670ca53" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186552900 #edb/ref 1080 "4.891" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186552900 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186552900 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "1298499f-9646-539b-b82a-129de42835ab" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186552963 #edb/ref 1080 "-0.126" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186552963 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186552963 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "31c08ec4-b598-5a54-a16a-1c8bee003ad2" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186552993 #edb/ref 1080 "\\frac{39}{20}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186552993 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186552993 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "3eaaf1c5-b2c0-59d7-bb44-f4a6