93 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186553483 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "f223b528-fa2a-51c1-a419-5e28eb4e3b2b" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186553490 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186553385 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186553490 #edb/ref 1069 "q-256513" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186553490 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186553490 #edb/ref 1071 "Suppose we wish to find a root of the function $f(x)=\\operatorname{cos}⁡x-\\frac{x-4}{5}$ in the interval $[4,5].$ Calculate one iteration of the Newton-Raphson process starting from the point ${x}_{0}=4.8.$ Round your answer to three decimal places.\n\n${x}_{1}≈$\n{{field-1}}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186553490 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "02923e80-b323-5245-827a-ada028b30cf4" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186553490 #edb/ref 1074 "The formula for the Newton-Raphson method is\n\n$$\n{x}_{n+1}={x}_{n}-\\frac{f({x}_{n})}{{f}^{′}({x}_{n})}\n$$\n\nwhere ${f}^{′}({x}_{n})$ is the derivative of $f(x)$ evaluated at ${x}_{n}.$\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\n{f}^{′}(x)={(\\operatorname{cos}⁡x-\\frac{x-4}{5})}^{′}=-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-\\frac{1}{5}\n$$\n\nTherefore, our Newton-Raphson formula is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{n+1} & ={x}_{n}-\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡{x}_{n}-\\frac{{x}_{n}-4}{5}}{-\\operatorname{sin}⁡{x}_{n}-\\frac{1}{5}} \\\\  & ={x}_{n}+\\frac{5\\operatorname{cos}⁡{x}_{n}-{x}_{n}+4}{5\\operatorname{sin}⁡{x}_{n}+1}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nStarting with ${x}_{0}=4.8,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} & ={x}_{0}+\\frac{5\\operatorname{cos}⁡{x}_{0}-{x}_{0}+4}{5\\operatorname{sin}⁡{x}_{0}+1} \\\\  & =4.8+\\frac{5\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4.8)-4.8+4}{5\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4.8)+1} \\\\  & ≈4.891,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nrounded to three decimal places." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186553514 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186553383 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186553514 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186553459 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186553514 #edb/ref 1069 "q-256556" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186553514 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186553514 #edb/ref 1071 "Suppose we wish to find a root of the function $f(x)=3{e}^{x}-{x}^{2}+5x-2$ in the interval $[-1,1].$ Calculate the first two iterations of the Newton-Raphson process starting from the point ${x}_{0}=0.6.$ Round your answers to three decimal places.\n\n${x}_{1}≈$\n{{field-1}}\n$,\\,{x}_{2}≈$\n{{field-2}}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186553514 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "3371c40e-35a5-55e7-a0b3-a7349d729101" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186553514 #edb/ref 1074 "The formula for the Newton-Raphson method is\n\n$$\n{x}_{n+1}={x}_{n}-\\frac{f({x}_{n})}{{f}^{′}({x}_{n})}\n$$\n\nwhere ${f}^{′}({x}_{n})$ is the derivative of $f(x)$ evaluated at ${x}_{n}.$\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\n{f}^{′}(x)=(3{e}^{x}-{x}^{2}+5x-2)^{′}=3{e}^{x}-2x+5.\n$$\n\nTherefore, our Newton-Raphson formula is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{n+1} & ={x}_{n}-\\frac{3{e}^{{x}_{n}}-{x}_{n}^{2}+5{x}_{n}-2}{3{e}^{{x}_{n}}-2{x}_{n}+5} \\\\  & =\\frac{{x}_{n}(3{e}^{{x}_{n}}-2{x}_{n}+5)-(3{e}^{{x}_{n}}-{x}_{n}^{2}+5{x}_{n}-2)}{3{e}^{{x}_{n}}-2{x}_{n}+5} \\\\  & =\\frac{3{x}_{n}{e}^{{x}_{n}}-{x}_{n}^{2}-3{e}^{{x}_{n}}+2}{3{e}^{{x}_{n}}-2{x}_{n}+5}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nStarting with ${x}_{0}=0.6,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} & =\\frac{3{x}_{0}{e}^{{x}_{0}}-{x}_{0}^{2}-3{e}^{{x}_{0}}+2}{3{e}^{{x}_{0}}-2{x}_{0}+5} \\\\  & =\\frac{3\\cdot 0.6{e}^{0.6}-(0.6)^{2}-3{e}^{0.6}+2}{3{e}^{0.6}-2\\cdot 0.6+5} \\\\  & =-0.058\\,981….\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFor the second iteration, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{2} & =\\frac{3{x}_{1}{e}^{{x}_{1}}-{x}_{1}^{2}-3{e}^{{x}_{1}}+2}{3{e}^{{x}_{1}}-2{x}_{1}+5} \\\\  & =\\frac{3\\cdot (-0.058\\,981…){e}^{-0.058\\,981…}-(-0.058\\,981…)^{2}-3{e}^{-0.058\\,981…}+2}{3{e}^{-0.058\\,981…}-2\\cdot (-0.058\\,981…)+5} \\\\  & =-0.125\\,654….\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, ${x}_{1}≈-0.059$ and ${x}_{2}≈-0.126,$ rounded to three decimal places." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186553535 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186553483 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186553535 #edb/ref 1069 "q-256471" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186553535 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186553535 #edb/ref 1071 "Suppose we wish to find a root of the function $f(x)={x}^{4}+{x}^{3}-2$ in the interval $[0,2].$ Calculate one iteration of the Newton-Raphson process starting from the point ${x}_{0}=0.5.$\n\n${x}_{1}=$\n{{field-1}}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186553535 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "6fa3586a-bc79-59ff-837c-430b6731e94e" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186553535 #edb/ref 1074 "The formula for the Newton-Raphson method is\n\n$$\n{x}_{n+1}={x}_{n}-\\frac{f({x}_{n})}{{f}^{′}({x}_{n})}\n$$\n\nwhere ${f}^{′}({x}_{n})$ is the derivative of $f(x)$ evaluated at ${x}_{n}.$\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\n{f}^{′}(x)=({x}^{4}+{x}^{3}-2)^{′}=4{x}^{3}+3{x}^{2}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, our Newton-Raphson formula is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{n+1} & ={x}_{n}-\\frac{{x}_{n}^{4}+{x}_{n}^{3}-2}{4{x}_{n}^{3}+3{x}_{n}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{{x}_{n}(4{x}_{n}^{3}+3{x}_{n}^{2})-({x}_{n}^{4}+{x}_{n}^{3}-2)}{4{x}_{n}^{3}+3{x}_{n}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{3{x}_{n}^{4}+2{x}_{n}^{3}+2}{4{x}_{n}^{3}+3{x}_{n}^{2}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nStarting with ${x}_{0}=0.5,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} & =\\frac{3{x}_{0}^{4}+2{x}_{0}^{3}+2}{4{x}_{0}^{3}+3{x}_{0}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{3(0.5)^{4}+2(0.5)^{3}+2}{4(0.5)^{3}+3(0.5)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{2.4375}{1.25} \\\\  & =1.95.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417]}
